// dbarrel_hands.h - the DOUBLE-BARREL wn_shotgun_a's manual-reload hand data + pure helpers (unit-tested:
// src/src/tests/dbarrel_logic_test.cpp). Spec docs/superpowers/specs/2026-11-04-manual-reload-pump-shotgun-design.md section 9.
// The tables are GENERATED by tools/dbarrel_anim_export.py (Blender) into reload_dbarrel_anim.inc - never edit them by hand:
//   kDbOpen[1]  Jay's open-step hand over the barrels, on the CLOSED gun (hand_top/pose_A_JAY.json, "Approved"); the hand that rides
//               the barrels at angle a = MeshHinge(a) x kDbOpen[0].hand (closing = the same grip reversed, Jay).
//   kDbPull[22] Jay's spent-shell pull-out (dbarrel_hold_H10_SMOOTH.blend, "Approved"), 60 fps, gun open 45 deg. It STARTS 10 mm out of
//               the bore (the "H10" key - the generator measured frame 1's shells 10.0 mm from the seat): the driver eases the shells
//               seat -> frame 1 while the hand locks on (the lock's 100 ms blend).
//   kDbLoad[49] the loading (dbarrel_load_r240_FAST.blend, "Approved"), 60 fps, gun open 45: shell 1 seats LEFT at kDbLoadSeatFrame[0],
//               shell 2 RIGHT at kDbLoadSeatFrame[1]; a 1-shell load into the right chamber plays from kDbLoadOneStart.
//   kDbSeat[2]  each shell element seated, in bone_reload_shotgun's frame.
// Matrices: row-major 3x4, basis = columns, t = [3] [7] [11] (reload.cpp's convention). No game access, no logging, no allocation.
